sections.body:
The `<canvas>` tag in HTML is an empty drawing canvas. To draw on it, we first ask it for a **brush** (the drawing context):

```js
const canvas = document.querySelector("#game");
const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
```

`ctx` is now the object that knows all the drawing commands. The canvas size is set in HTML with `width` and `height`: `<canvas id="game" width="300" height="200">`. In code you read these values with `canvas.width` and `canvas.height`.

Circles and lines are drawn as a **path**: start with `beginPath()`, describe the shape, then say `fill()` or `stroke()`:

```js
ctx.beginPath();
ctx.arc(150, 100, 30, 0, Math.PI * 2); // center x, y, radius, full turn
ctx.fillStyle = "#ff9800";
ctx.fill();

ctx.beginPath();
ctx.moveTo(10, 190);  // put the pen here
ctx.lineTo(290, 190); // draw up to here
ctx.strokeStyle = "white";
ctx.stroke();

ctx.fillStyle = "white";
ctx.font = "16px sans-serif";
ctx.fillText("Star Hunter", 10, 20);
```

The real power is drawing the picture **from data**: you run the same command in a loop for every item of an array. When the array changes, the picture changes too:

```js
const stars = [{ x: 40, y: 30 }, { x: 120, y: 80 }, { x: 250, y: 50 }];
ctx.fillStyle = "#f7df1e";
for (const star of stars) {
  ctx.fillRect(star.x, star.y, 6, 6);
}
```

examples.code:
const ctx = document.querySelector("#sky").getContext("2d");

// Sky
ctx.fillStyle = "#0b1026";
ctx.fillRect(0, 0, 300, 160);

// Moon
ctx.beginPath();
ctx.arc(240, 40, 22, 0, Math.PI * 2);
ctx.fillStyle = "#fff5c0";
ctx.fill();

// Ground
ctx.fillStyle = "#2e7d32";
ctx.fillRect(0, 130, 300, 30);

// Rocket: fill and outline
ctx.fillStyle = "#e53935";
ctx.fillRect(60, 80, 16, 50);
ctx.strokeStyle = "white";
ctx.strokeRect(60, 80, 16, 50);

// Text
ctx.fillStyle = "white";
ctx.font = "14px sans-serif";
ctx.fillText("Pixel Planet", 10, 20);

const canvas = document.querySelector("#sky");
const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
ctx.fillStyle = "#0b1026";
ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);

// 40 random stars
ctx.fillStyle = "white";
for (let i = 0; i < 40; i++) {
  const x = Math.random() * canvas.width;
  const y = Math.random() * canvas.height;
  ctx.fillRect(x, y, 2, 2);
}

// Planets from an array
const planets = [
  { x: 60, y: 90, r: 25, color: "#ff9800" },
  { x: 150, y: 50, r: 15, color: "#4fc3f7" },
  { x: 235, y: 100, r: 35, color: "#e53935" },
];
for (const p of planets) {
  ctx.beginPath();
  ctx.arc(p.x, p.y, p.r, 0, Math.PI * 2);
  ctx.fillStyle = p.color;
  ctx.fill();
}

